import json, sys, collections
S = sys.argv[1]
cells = json.load(open(S + '/work/cells_computed.json', encoding='utf-8'))
out = json.load(open(S + '/dayton_cell_assignments.json', encoding='utf-8'))['cells']
rows = json.load(open(S + '/work/summary_rows.json', encoding='utf-8'))
diff = json.load(open(S + '/work/diff_rows.json', encoding='utf-8'))
war = json.load(open(S + '/work/wartime_controllers.json', encoding='utf-8'))

tot = collections.Counter(c['confidence'] for c in out.values())
L = []
w = L.append

w("# Dayton IEBL per-cell audit (historian seat, 2026-11-08)")
w("")
w("Read-only research output. Nothing inside any repository or worktree was modified. Companion file: `dayton_cell_assignments.json` (schema `dayton_cell_assignments/v1`, 252 cells).")
w("")
w(f"**Totals:** {len(out)} cells in scope; confidence verified {tot['verified']}, approximate {tot['approximate']}, unresolved {tot['unresolved']}.")
w("")
w("## 1. Method")
w("")
w("1. **Enumeration.** Every cell id (`op:<mun>:<cell>`) in `data/derived/operational/osid_areas.json` whose middle segment is one of the 34 municipalities in scope (28 split municipalities + Srebrenica, Bratunac, Čajniče, Rogatica (holds Žepa; there is no `zepa` municipality key), Višegrad, Brčko). 252 cells, all present in `operational_settlements.geojson`.")
w("2. **The IEBL at settlement resolution.** The repo already holds the implemented IEBL, although not under that name: `data/source/bih_census_1991.json` is the 1991 census as republished by the BiH Agency for Statistics on the post-1995 (Dayton) municipal structure. Every 1991 settlement carries the post-1995 municipality code (`1xxxx` = Federation, `2xxxx` = Republika Srpska, `3xxxx` = Brčko District). Settlements cut by the IEBL appear twice, once per side, with the population of each part (e.g. Trnovo 114 FBiH / 1,985 RS; Prača 710 FBiH / 314 RS). The post-1995 municipal boundaries *are* the IEBL inside split pre-war municipalities, so this gives the line at settlement resolution, which is finer than the cells.")
w("3. **Join.** cell -> `constituent_sids` -> `settlements_wgs84_1990.geojson` (`census_ids`) -> census code -> entity. Each member settlement's polygon area (km², shoelace on a local equirectangular projection) is attributed to its entity; split settlements are attributed in proportion to the BHAS population split. Result per cell: area share and population share per entity, listed in `work/cells_computed.json` and `work/crossed_cells.txt`.")
w("4. **Rules applied** (recorded in each cell's `rule` field):")
w("   - `A2-SETTLEMENT`: all member settlements lie in one post-1995 municipality -> that entity, confidence *verified*.")
w("   - `A2-MAJORITY-AREA x%`: the cell is crossed by the IEBL; it goes to the side holding the larger area. *Verified* when the minority share is under 15 %, *approximate* otherwise.")
w("   - `A2-PRINCIPAL-SETTLEMENT override`: used only when the area majority is below 60 % **and** both the population majority and the cell's principal settlement (namesake / largest town) lie on the other side. Applied to 6 cells (Domaljevac, Kolovarice, Gornji Svilaj, Podgrab, Prača, Pješivac-Kula).")
w("   - *Unresolved*: area majority >= 60 % but population majority and principal settlement on the other side (Oštra Luka/Donji Žabar, Stari Majdan, Veličani/Ravno, Tošići, Trnovo). The entity field carries the area-rule answer; the owner decides.")
w("   - `FED-LAYER`: inside the Federation the faction follows the existing RULE-FED-LAYER convention of `plan_maps_research.json` (party administering the ground at war end / Washington cantonal arrangement; Croat-majority cantons 2, 8, 10 and HDZ-run municipalities of mixed cantons 6 and 7 -> HRHB; otherwise RBiH). The canton membership is documented (Law on Federal Units, 12 Jun 1996); the HDZ-run reading of Jajce, Dobretići, Stolac and Ravno is an inference and caps those cells at *approximate*. Mostar is assigned per cell from the ICTY Prlić judgement front line and the Feb 1996 Interim Statute (three Croat west, three Bosniak east city-municipalities).")
w("   - `A2-ART-V`: all 13 Brčko cells are `special`; Annex 2 Art. V put the disputed line to arbitration and the Final Award (5 Mar 1999, para 11) made the entire pre-war opština the District. The interim 1995-2000 RS/Federation portion of each cell is noted in `evidence`.")
w("5. **Wartime control** (`political.political_controllers` of the reference save) was used only for the difference list in §5. That save is an *emergent* RS run at turn 104 (~April 1994), not a historical end-state, so differences are expected and not all of them are Dayton transfers.")
w("")
w("## 2. Sources consulted")
w("")
w("Primary / judicial first, then BB, then secondary, per the historian source rule.")
w("")
w("- **GFAP Annex 2** (Agreement on Inter-Entity Boundary Line and Related Issues), Arts I-VII and Appendix: https://www.ohr.int/dayton-peace-agreement/annex-2/ (fetched; Art. V arbitration text and the 'administered as currently' clause quoted from it).")
w("- **Brčko Arbitral Tribunal, Final Award, 5 Mar 1999**: https://www.ohr.int/?p=111275 (fetched). Para 9: each entity delegates its powers within the pre-war Brčko opština; para 11: the whole opština is held in condominium; para 39: 'the RS portion and the Federation portion of the Brcko Opstina' continue under their laws until harmonised.")
w("- **ICTY Prlić et al., Trial Judgement IT-04-74-T, 29 May 2013, Vol. 2** (https://www.icty.org/x/cases/prlic/tjug/en/130529-2.pdf, fetched and text-extracted): para 782 (Mostar front line along the Bulevar and Šantićeva Street, ABiH east of it), para 917 (HVO-ABiH fighting at Buna, Gubavica, Lakševine, July 1993), para 991 (East Mostar and connected sectors, notably Blagaj, under siege Jun 1993 - Apr 1994), para 694 fn 1552 (HV 8th Light Assault Bde in Buna), para 1897 (HVO 1st Knez Domagoj Bde took Stolac June 1992), Stolac chapter (removal of Muslims Jul-Aug 1993).")
w("- **UN A/54/549** (Fall of Srebrenica) for the enclave outcome, as already cited in `plan_maps_research.json`.")
w("- **Balkan Battlegrounds KB** (`data/derived/knowledge_base/balkan_battlegrounds/pages`, KB page ids): BB1 p0175 (Ustikolina, Apr 1992), p0182 (VRS takes Odžak 12 Jul 1992), p0217 and p0437 (HVO Orašje pocket; 202nd Home Defence Regt Domaljevac-Grebnice, 106th at Oštra Luka), p0419-0420 (ARBiH 5th Corps takes Petrovac, Ključ 17 Sep, drive on Sanski Most; HV/HVO toward Jajce), p0439 (VRS sectors opposite Teočak and Sapna, 1995), p0442 (SRK 1st Sarajevo Mech Bde vic. Grbavica-Lukavica), p0443 (Treskavica-Trnovo 1995), p0500 (VRS 3rd Posavina LIB HQ Pelagićevo), p0509 and p0514 (ARBiH brigades at Klokotnica, Čelić, Teočak, Kalesija, Sapna); BB2 p0401 (208th Čelić Bde, 107th Gradačac Bde), p0409-0410 (Ustiprača line 1993; Trnovo-Goražde corridor, Jabuka-Grebak route), p0478-0479 (VRS advance through Kopači, Apr 1994), p0481 (Prača Battalion), p0490-0491 ('Sapna thumb' 1994), p0527 (Kupres falls to HVO/ARBiH 3 Nov 1994).")
w("- **Repo data**: `data/source/bih_census_1991.json` (BHAS 1991 census on post-1995 borders), `data/source/municipality_post1995_to_mun1990.json` (142 post-1995 municipalities, names/codes), `data/derived/settlements_wgs84_1990.geojson`, `data/derived/operational/operational_settlements.geojson`, `data/derived/operational/osid_areas.json`, `data/source/peace_plans/plan_maps_research.json` (dayton entries, RULE-FED-LAYER), `docs/40_reports/20261107_PEACE_PLANS_RESEARCH.md` §6.")
w("- **Secondary cross-checks (Wikipedia raw wikitext, fetched)**: 'Inter-Entity Boundary Line' (table of FBiH/RS municipality pairs, matches the BHAS pairing exactly), 'Bosnian-Podrinje Canton Goražde' (municipalities Goražde, Foča-Ustikolina, Pale-Prača), 'Brčko District' (Final Award date 5 Mar 1999; Statute 8 Mar 2000), 'Goražde' ('After the Dayton Agreement, a land corridor was established between Goražde and the Federation'), 'Siege of Goražde' (split into Novo Goražde RS / Goražde FBiH), 'Mostar' (Feb 1996 Interim Statute: six city-municipalities, three Croat west, three Bosniak east, plus a Central Zone), 'Cantons of the Federation of BiH' (Law on Federal Units 12 Jun 1996; 5 Bosniak-majority, 3 Croat-majority, 2 mixed cantons).")
w("")
w("Not reachable or not used: the 1:50,000 Annex 2 Appendix map sheets themselves (not online); OHR's Mostar Interim Statute text (not located); Wikipedia stubs for Rahić-Brčko / Ravne-Brčko (rate-limited). The pre-2000 Brčko portions are therefore recorded from Final Award para 39 plus the ceasefire geography, as *approximate* notes only.")
w("")
w("## 3. Per-municipality summary")
w("")
w("Area shares are over the cells as assigned (whole cells), so they differ from the polygon-exact shares in `plan_maps_research.json`.")
w("")
w("| Municipality | Cells | Entity (cells) | Faction (cells) | Area share by assigned entity | Verified | Approx. | Unresolved |")
w("|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
for r in rows:
    ents = ', '.join(f"{k} {v}" for k, v in sorted(r['entities'].items()))
    facs = ', '.join(f"{k} {v}" for k, v in sorted(r['factions'].items()))
    area = ', '.join(f"{k} {v}%" for k, v in sorted(r['area_share'].items()))
    w(f"| {r['mun']} | {r['cells']} | {ents} | {facs} | {area} | {r['verified']} | {r['approximate']} | {r['unresolved']} |")
w(f"| **Total** | **{len(out)}** | | | | **{tot['verified']}** | **{tot['approximate']}** | **{tot['unresolved']}** |")
w("")
w("### 3.1 Cells crossed by the IEBL (minority share >= 3 %)")
w("")
w("| Cell | Area FED/RS % | Pop FED/RS % | Assigned | Rule | Confidence |")
w("|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
for o in sorted(out):
    v = cells[o]; sa = v['share_area']
    if len(sa) < 2 or min(sa.values()) < 3 or v['mun'] == 'brcko':
        continue
    sp = v['share_pop']
    w(f"| {o} | {sa.get('FED', 0)}/{sa.get('RS', 0)} | {sp.get('FED', 0)}/{sp.get('RS', 0)} | {out[o]['entity']}/{out[o]['faction']} | {out[o]['rule'].split(';')[0]} | {out[o]['confidence']} |")
w("")
w("## 4. Enclaves, corridor and Brčko (history only, no game rule proposed)")
w("")
w("**Srebrenica** (13 cells) and **Bratunac** (8): wholly RS at Dayton. The Srebrenica safe area fell to the VRS on 11 July 1995 (A/54/549; BB1 KB p0432-0435); Dayton confirmed RS control of the whole municipality. **Žepa** (`op:rogatica:zepa_2`, inside Rogatica) fell on 25 July 1995 (BB1 KB p0444-0448) and the whole of Rogatica is RS. **Čajniče, Višegrad**: wholly RS.")
w("")
w("**Goražde**: the enclave stayed with the Federation and was joined to it by a land corridor. In the data this is the Bosnian-Podrinje Canton Goražde = Goražde (FBiH, code 11452) + Foča-Ustikolina (11444) + Pale-Prača (11576). RS kept Novo Goražde (20419: Kopači, Ustiprača, the right-bank villages east and south-east of the town; VRS-held since the April 1994 offensive, BB2 KB p0478-0479). Note the repo xlsx names both Goražde parts 'Novo Goražde'; the BHAS codes disambiguate (1475355/11452 Goražde FBiH vs 1255549/20419 Novo Goražde RS).")
w("")
w("Cells that form the corridor between Goražde and the Sarajevo canton (Federation side, west to east): `op:trnovo:tusila`, `op:trnovo:delijas`, `op:trnovo:gornja_presjenica` (Trnovo FBiH, the Treskavica side) -> `op:foca:donje_zesce`, `op:foca:mazlina`, `op:foca:ustikolina` (Foča-Ustikolina; the wartime Jabuka-Grebak trail of BB2 KB p0410 runs through `op:foca:izbisno`, whose FBiH settlements Jabuka, Lokve, Zabor and Slavičići are outvoted by RS area in that cell) -> Goražde cells. The Prača valley arm is `op:pale:praca`, `op:pale:vrazalice`, `op:pale:bulozi` and the FBiH part of `op:pale:podgrab`. The exact Dayton corridor road alignment is documented only at municipality level here; the cell list is *approximate*.")
w("")
w("**Brčko**: Annex 2 Art. V left the disputed IEBL portion to binding arbitration and kept the area 'administered as currently'; the 1995-2000 Dayton line left Brčko town and the Sava corridor north of it in RS and the south of the municipality in the Federation (Rahić-Brčko, Bosniak-run; Ravne-Brčko, Croat-run, in the west). The Final Award of 5 March 1999 (para 11) made **the entire pre-war opština** the Brčko District in condominium, established 8 March 2000. Therefore all 13 cells are `special`, and all 13 became District. Interim-side notes per cell are in `evidence`.")
w("")
w("## 5. Cells where the Dayton assignment differs from the wartime controller in the reference save")
w("")
w(f"{len(diff)} of 252 cells. The save is an emergent RS run at turn 104 (~Apr 1994), so this list mixes (a) genuine Dayton transfers against the end-1995 line, (b) the save's own divergence from history (e.g. Petrovac, Ključ, Sanski Most, Drvar, Kupres and Jajce are still RS at turn 104 but were taken by the ARBiH/HV/HVO in Sept-Oct 1995 and Nov 1994; the eastern enclaves are still RBiH), and (c) all Brčko cells (special). Faction-level differences inside the Federation are included.")
w("")
w("| Cell | Wartime (save t104) | Dayton entity | Faction | Confidence |")
w("|---|---|---|---|---|")
for d in diff:
    w(f"| {d['osid']} | {d['wartime']} | {d['entity']} | {d['faction']} | {d['confidence']} |")
w("")
w("**Known defect confirmed.** `op:zvornik:sapna` (Vitinica, Sapna, Zaseok, Kraljevići, Nezuk, Međeđa: all Sapna FBiH; 81.8 % of area, 92.5 % of population) and `op:ugljevik:teocak_krstac_2` (all five settlements in Teočak FBiH) are Federation/RBiH. Both were ARBiH-held throughout the war (BB1 KB p0439, p0514; BB2 KB p0490-0491). The quota pass's RS assignment is wrong for both.")
w("")
w("## 6. Where sources disagree, and open questions for the owner")
w("")
w("1. **Trnovo town.** Research report v1 (§6.3) says 'the town of Trnovo to the Federation'. The BHAS structure puts the Trnovo settlement 1,985 RS / 114 FBiH, i.e. the town is in Trnovo (RS); the FBiH municipality of the same name is the Dejčići-Trebečaj-Ledići valley to the west. The cell `op:trnovo:trnovo` is 79 % FBiH by area but RS by town and population: **unresolved**, owner decision. The v1 note should be corrected.")
w("2. **Unresolved cells (5)**: `op:orasje:ostra_luka` (Donji Žabar RS seat vs Oštra Luka/Bok FBiH, population 51/49), `op:sanski_most:stari_majdan` (74 % RS land, but Stari Majdan town FBiH), `op:trebinje:velicani` (62 % RS land, Ravno seat FBiH), `op:trnovo:tosici`, `op:trnovo:trnovo`. Recommend the owner pick either the area rule or the principal-settlement rule for all five consistently.")
w("3. **Principal-settlement overrides (6)**: Domaljevac, Kolovarice, Gornji Svilaj, Podgrab, Prača, Pješivac-Kula. Each is recorded with both indicators; flipping them to the area rule changes about 406 km² in total.")
w("4. **Mostar faction layer.** The research JSON's 'Federation/split' (half RBiH, half HRHB) is replaced by per-cell: RBiH 6 cells (east bank, north valley, Blagaj, Podveležje, Drežnica, Vranjevići), HRHB 3 (west bank, Jasenica/Buna right bank, Hodbina-Gubavica). Hodbina-Gubavica (Bosniak villages taken by the HVO in July 1993) and Drežnica (ARBiH valley with HVO Croat villages Goranci/Bogodol in the same cell) are the weakest calls.")
w("5. **Jajce as HRHB** follows the existing RULE-FED-LAYER (HDZ-run after HV/HVO retook the town in Sept 1995). The pre-war plurality was Bosniak and the ARBiH 7th Corps fought alongside; if the owner prefers 'liberating force' over 'administering party', Jajce's 8 FBiH cells are the ones that move.")
w("6. **Ilidža/Sarajevo suburbs.** Entity is documented (OHR 1996 transfers). The reference save shows them RS; the Dayton map transfers them to the Federation. No disagreement among sources.")
w("7. **Odžak** was VRS-held from 12 July 1992 (BB1 KB p0182) and went to the Federation at Dayton: the research JSON's 'inferred' control date is now BB-documented.")
w("8. **Brčko interim portions** (which cells were RS-administered 1995-2000) are from ceasefire geography, not from the Appendix map: approximate notes only; the District outcome is documented.")
w("9. **Area weighting of split settlements** uses the BHAS population split as a proxy for the area split (no settlement-part polygons exist). Sensitivity check: under the alternative of splitting each cut settlement's area 50/50, five cells change or tie their area majority: `op:kupres:novo_selo_2` (RS 77.5 % -> FED 57.1 %: the three cut settlements Mrđanovci, Novo Selo, Šemenovci are almost wholly RS by population, so the population weighting is the better reading, but the cell is flagged), `op:trebinje:velicani` and `op:trnovo:tosici` (already unresolved), `op:gradacac:donja_tramosnica_2` and `op:lopare:jablanica_2` (exact 50/50 ties; population 84 % and 91 % RS, assignment RS kept). All five are marked approximate or unresolved.")
w("10. The `plan_maps_research.json` xlsx-derived name 'Novo Goražde' for the FBiH part of Goražde should read 'Goražde' (BHAS 1475355 / code 11452).")
w("")
w("## 7. Files")
w("")
w("- `dayton_cell_assignments.json`: the deliverable (252 cells).")
w("- `work/compute_cells.py`, `work/build_outputs.py`, `work/build_audit_md.py`: deterministic pipeline (reads repo data read-only).")
w("- `work/cells_computed.json`, `work/cells_summary.txt`, `work/crossed_cells.txt`: per-cell settlement-level evidence.")
w("- `work/wartime_controllers.json`, `work/diff_rows.json`: reference-save comparison.")
w("- `dl/`: fetched sources (Annex 2, Final Award, Prlić TJ Vol. 2 PDF + text, Wikipedia raw wikitext).")
open(S + '/AUDIT.md', 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(L) + '\n')
print('AUDIT.md written', len(L), 'lines')
